<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grameen Bank</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1983</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Grameen Bank is a microfinance organisation in Bangladesh that makes small loans without collateral to poor people, most of them rural women. Begun as a project by the economist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-yunus">Muhammad Yunus</a> in 1976 and established as a bank in 1983, it pioneered group lending and influenced microcredit programmes worldwide. Yunus and the bank shared the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-peace-prize">Nobel Peace Prize</a> in 2006.</p></div>
